<title>GREECE: EMPLOYEES STAGE WALKOUT AT ALUMINIUM OF GREECE PLANT.</title>
<headline>EMPLOYEES STAGE WALKOUT AT ALUMINIUM OF GREECE PLANT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aluminium of Greece employees at Aspra Spitia plant in central Greece staged a walkout today protesting against the non-replacement of workers who retired, sources said.</p>
<p>Employees will repeat the walkout this weekend, the sources said.</p>
<p>&quot;The walkout is not justified,&quot; a company official told Reuters. &quot;The voluntary retirement plan aims at the survival of the company and its long-term competitiveness.&quot; --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
